5851: metadata remains in the primary source.  This gate is a local readiness
5852: certificate only; it does not assert final-upload-time venue compliance,
5853: EasyChair upload, reviewer approval, acceptance, camera-ready approval, or
5854: proceedings publication.  A future stronger reading requires the additional
5855: upload-time finite record specified in
5856: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-time-venue-compliance-record-requirement} and
5857: Theorem~\ref{thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation}.
5858: \end{proposition}
5859: 
5860: 
5861: \medskip
5862: \begin{proof}
5863: The table has five rows, so the check is finite.  The route-class row compares
5864: the venue's presentation-only rule with the local role separation already fixed
5865: by Proposition~\ref{prop:final-package-shape-convention}:
5866: \path{submission_abstract.tex} is primary, while \path{main.tex},
5867: \path{theorem_inventory.json}, and \path{review_bundle/} are local support
5868: artifacts.  If the primary artifact is not the short source, if those
5869: support artifacts are presented as a second primary proceedings paper, or if the
5870: bundle branch is silently changed to an unrecorded archive replacement, this row
5871: fails.  If it passes, the row proves only compatibility with the
5872: presentation-only artifact split, because its
5873: boundary column expressly excludes acceptance and proceedings-publication
5874: claims.
5875: 
5876: The formatting row is a syntactic source check.  The manuscript begins with the
5877: LNCS class \path{llncs}; the package uses \path{splncs04} for the bibliography;
5878: and the local compiled short artifact and bibliography files are present as
5879: \path{submission_abstract.pdf} and \path{submission_abstract.bbl}.  These are
5880: finite path and token checks.  They do not inspect Springer production systems,
5881: nor do they prove that the venue will accept the formatting; hence the row gives
5882: local formatting readiness only.  The supplement-access row is finite because it
5883: requires the selected exact bundle files, the final digest manifest, and the
5884: root theorem-inventory coordinate named by the manifest and certificate ledger.
5885: Audit record~\ref{audit:review-bundle-archive-equivalence} remains only the
5886: criterion that would have to be satisfied by a future archive replacement; it is
5887: not the branch selected by the current source package.  The metadata and
5888: bibliography row checks the title, author block, institute/email block,
5889: bibliography command, and \path{references.bib}; it does not certify external
5890: metadata entry.  The deadline row records only that the package can be checked
5891: against the venue date before upload and does not assert that an upload was made.
5892: 
5893: If all rows pass, each venue-facing pre-upload checklist claim used by this
5894: manuscript has a finite local witness and an explicit negative boundary, so the
5895: package is ready in the limited local sense stated in the proposition.
5896: Conversely, if any row fails, one of the finite route-class, formatting,
5897: supplement-access, metadata, bibliography, or deadline witnesses required by the
5898: table is absent or stale; there is then no local certificate for submission-pack
5899: readiness.  Because the hypothesis deliberately omits an upload receipt,
5900: completed-upload timestamp, archive-equivalent locator, and unchanged-rule
5901: statement for a completed upload, no row can identify the venue-rule state at
5902: the actual upload event.  The final sentence follows from the boundary column,
5903: Corollary~\ref{cor:upload-time-venue-compliance-record-requirement}, and
5904: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface}: external upload,
5905: upload-time compliance, acceptance, camera-ready approval, and publication are
5906: editorial or venue events, not local finite-record consequences of this gate.
5907: \end{proof}
5908: 
5909: \begin{proposition}[Submission artifact role separation]
5910: \label{audit:submission-artifact-role-separation}
5911: For the current presentation-only route, the primary artifact, long technical
5912: supplement, and review bundle have distinct review roles.  The primary source
5913: \path{submission_abstract.tex} states the presentation claim, \path{main.tex}
5914: proves the long-form interface theorems and records the case tables, and
5915: \path{review_bundle/} supplies the supplemental source snapshots, case snapshots,
5916: and machine-readable manifest rows.  None of these roles converts the support
5917: bundle into a second primary submission or converts a primary-artifact claim into
5918: an uncited supplement claim.
5919: \end{proposition}
5920: 
5921: 
5922: \medskip
5923: \begin{proof}
5924: The manifest field \path{submission_artifacts} names the short source, intended
5925: short PDF, long technical source, long technical PDF, and supplemental bundle as
5926: separate artifacts.  The checklist above fixes how the short artifact points to
5927: the supplement: it names the safety theorem, the case rows, the evidence-level
5928: boundary, and \path{review_bundle/}.  The earlier source-snapshot and
5929: case-snapshot propositions identify the two support functions of the bundle: a
5930: pinned discovery-gate source snapshot and bounded case-evidence snapshots.  Since
5931: the primary note states only the interface and each support claim is tied to a
5932: specific theorem, table, or manifest field, the artifacts remain role-separated:
5933: the support materials make the primary note reviewable but do not become hidden
5934: primary claims.\end{proof}
